The graphs of $f(x)=x^2$ and $g(x)=\dfrac{1}{x-1}+1$ are shown below.

\exfigure{1597_q2a_1}

Which graph best represents $y=f(g(x))$? Circle the correct alternative.

solutions.latex:
The curve oscillates between $2$ and $6$ about $y=4$, starting at $(0,2)$, with maxima at $x=\dfrac{\pi}{2}$ and $\dfrac{3\pi}{2}$ and minima at $x=\pi$ and $2\pi$.

\exfigure{1597_q2c_s1}

Period $=\pi$, amplitude $=2$.
